# One line-ending convention, everywhere: LF in the index, LF in the working tree, on every
# machine. Without this, a file committed from Windows keeps its CRLF and then re-diffs
# whole-file the first time it is touched from the Mac -- the churn that made a generated
# requirements.txt look like a real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text. `text=auto` already detects these, but saying
# it out loud costs nothing and survives a file that fools the heuristic.
*.png binary
*.PNG binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Parked evidence, left exactly as it is. These are byte-for-byte copies of 673f7a0 and their
# README records the CRLF endings as one of the findings, so normalizing them would quietly
# delete the thing they were kept to show.
test-vehicles/dockerignore-check/** -text
